{
    "map": {
        "config_keyword.descr": "The configuration keyword applies to enterprise geodatabase data only. It determines the storage parameters of the database table.",
        "config_keyword.title": "Configuration Keyword",
        "description": "Creates an empty feature class in a geodatabase or a shapefile in a folder.",
        "geometry_type.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the geometry type of the output feature class.</p><ul><li><span title=\"POINT\">Point</span>—The geometry type will be point.</li><li><span title=\"MULTIPOINT\">Multipoint</span>—The geometry type will be multipoint.</li><li><span title=\"POLYGON\">Polygon</span>—The geometry type will be polygon.</li><li><span title=\"POLYLINE\">Polyline</span>—The geometry type will be polyline.</li><li><span title=\"MULTIPATCH\">Multipatch</span>—The geometry type will be multipatch.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "geometry_type.domain.MULTIPATCH": "Multipatch",
        "geometry_type.domain.MULTIPOINT": "Multipoint",
        "geometry_type.domain.POINT": "Point",
        "geometry_type.domain.POLYGON": "Polygon",
        "geometry_type.domain.POLYLINE": "Polyline",
        "geometry_type.title": "Geometry Type",
        "has_m.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the feature class will have linear measurement values (m-values).</p><ul><li><span title=\"DISABLED\">No</span>—The output feature class will not have m-values. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"ENABLED\">Yes</span>—The output feature class will have m-values.</li><li><span title=\"SAME_AS_TEMPLATE\">Same as the template feature class</span>—The output feature class will have m-values if the dataset specified in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Template Feature Class</span> parameter (template parameter in Python) has m-values.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "has_m.domain.DISABLED": "No",
        "has_m.domain.ENABLED": "Yes",
        "has_m.domain.SAME_AS_TEMPLATE": "Same as the template feature class",
        "has_m.title": "Has M",
        "has_z.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the feature class will have elevation values (z-values).</p><ul><li><span title=\"DISABLED\">No</span>—The output feature class will not have z-values. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"ENABLED\">Yes</span>—The output feature class will have z-values.</li><li><span title=\"SAME_AS_TEMPLATE\">Same as the template feature class</span>—The output feature class will have z-values if the dataset specified in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Template Feature Class</span> parameter (template parameter in Python) has z-values.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "has_z.domain.DISABLED": "No",
        "has_z.domain.ENABLED": "Yes",
        "has_z.domain.SAME_AS_TEMPLATE": "Same as the template feature class",
        "has_z.title": "Has Z",
        "oid_type.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the output Object ID field will be 32 bit or 64 bit.</p><ul><li><span title=\"SAME_AS_TEMPLATE\">Same as template</span>—The output Object ID field type (32 bit or 64 bit) will be the same as the Object ID field of the first template dataset. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"64_BIT\">64-bit</span>—The output Object ID field will be 64 bit.</li><li><span title=\"32_BIT\">32-bit</span>—The output Object ID field will be 32 bit.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "oid_type.domain.32_BIT": "32-bit",
        "oid_type.domain.64_BIT": "64-bit",
        "oid_type.domain.SAME_AS_TEMPLATE": "Same as template",
        "oid_type.title": "OID Type",
        "out_alias.descr": "The alternate name for the output feature class that will be created.",
        "out_alias.title": "Feature Class Alias",
        "out_feature_class.title": "Output Feature Class",
        "out_name.descr": "The name of the feature class to be created.",
        "out_name.title": "Feature Class Name",
        "out_path.descr": "The enterprise or file geodatabase or the folder in which the output feature class will be created. This workspace must already exist.",
        "out_path.title": "Feature Class Location",
        "params.category1": "Geodatabase Settings (optional)",
        "spatial_grid_1.descr": "This parameter is not supported. Any value provided will be ignored.",
        "spatial_grid_1.title": "Output Spatial Grid 1",
        "spatial_grid_2.descr": "This parameter is not supported. Any value provided will be ignored.",
        "spatial_grid_2.title": "Output Spatial Grid 2",
        "spatial_grid_3.descr": "This parameter is not supported. Any value provided will be ignored.",
        "spatial_grid_3.title": "Output Spatial Grid 3",
        "spatial_reference.descr": "<xdoc><p>The spatial reference of the output feature dataset. On the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Spatial Reference Properties</span> dialog box, you can select, import, or create a new coordinate system. To set aspects of the spatial reference, such as the x,y-, z-, or m-domain, resolution, or tolerance, use the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Environments</span> dialog box.</p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">This parameter is optional, but providing a value is recommended. If no spatial reference is provided, the output will have an undefined spatial reference.</p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">The spatial reference of the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Template Feature Class</span> value has no effect on the output spatial reference. If you want the output to be in the coordinate system of the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Template Feature Class</span> value, set the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Coordinate System</span> parameter to the spatial reference of the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Template Feature Class</span> value.</p></xdoc>",
        "spatial_reference.title": "Coordinate System",
        "template.descr": "An existing dataset or a list of datasets used as templates to define the attribute fields of the new feature class.",
        "template.title": "Template Datasets",
        "title": "Create Feature Class"
    }
}
